      "created_at": "2018-04-10T17:34:01.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm not sure if this has come and gone, but today's Progeny episode has got me thinking about the identity of Tim Cosing. &nbsp;I have a few anagrams, and a few notes first:</p><p>1. The proper name is between \"Progeny\" and \"Sanction.\" &nbsp;The only character with a name in this gap is Ra, and that seems somewhat unlikely to me. &nbsp;Minor nemeses in this gap are Revenant, Rahazar, Quetzacoatl, and Ruin (who's dead). &nbsp;Perhaps \"Rat Beast?\"</p><p>2. This new baddie interacts with Zhu Long as per the rule book (note that no reward clarifications are censored).</p><p>3. Anagrams!</p><p>- SMITING OC- An alternate (or \"original\") Fanatic?</p><p>- SMITING CO- An army general of some sort? &nbsp;Or maybe Vyktor's alter ego?</p><p>- MIST CON GI- Can we really trust Old Bunker? &nbsp;Or, dare I say it, Grandpa Legacy?</p><p>- MISTIC NOG- Could Santa Guise be deceiving us?</p><p>- OMNI CIGS T- Just saying, \"Reaper,\" as in the Omni-reaper, fits the name slot.</p><p>I checked all raw Caesar cyphers and all cyphers with Oblivaeon leading the alphabet and came up with nothing legible. &nbsp;Share any new discoveries, please!</p><p>(BTW if there's already like 1000 threads for this and one is still active, I'll happily move this there.)</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:08.776Z",
